process-spawn-at.m's process kind spawned on the machine's GPU
(docs/INPROGRESS.md, GPU processes without omp target, step 4c, and GPU
processes that run loops, one kernel for a GPU's processes): the runtime
loads the module's image through liboffload, sets its device number, and
starts the process in the image's kernel, which receives the host's messages through its
mailbox's ring and sends its answer back. The program ends when main does,
even while a GPU process waits for messages. A program compiled for another
GPU has no image for this one, which is a software error at the spawn.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/process-spawn-at.m -o %t2
RUN: %gpu-env %t2 gpu | FileCheck %S/process-spawn-at.m --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
RUN: merkc -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/process-spawn-at.m -o %t
RUN: %gpu-env %t gpu | FileCheck %S/process-spawn-at.m --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
RUN: %gpu-env %t2 leave | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LEAVE --match-full-lines
LEAVE:main ends

The runtime that stops the program while a GPU process runs leaves the
offload library to the process's end: its destructors would free the host
memory that the GPU's kernel reads, and the GPU would fault.
RUN: not %gpu-env %t2 closures 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CLOSURES
CLOSURES: Mercury runtime: called unify/2 for `pred' type
CLOSURES-NOT: memory access fault

RUN: merkc -O2 -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=gfx906 %libomp-flags %S/process-spawn-at.m -o %t.other
RUN: not %gpu-env %t.other gpu 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OTHER
OTHER: Software Error: process_spawn_at.spawn_summer_at: the module process_spawn_at has no image of its GPU process kinds for GPU 0, a {{gfx[0-9a-f]+}}: it must be compiled with --offload-arch={{gfx[0-9a-f]+}}

The messages that the GPU process took from its ring are freed, and so are
its arena and its mailbox's ring when it ends.
RUN: %gpu-env MERK_CHECK_MESSAGES=1 MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 %t2 gpu 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MESSAGES --match-full-lines
MESSAGES:Mercury runtime: 0 messages are neither read nor freed
MESSAGES-NEXT:Mercury runtime: 0 chunks of the devices' arenas and 0 rings are allocated

The GPU's processes run on the first pair of compute units that its queues
may use, on a queue limited to them (runtime/compute-units.h), which
LIBOMPTARGET_AMDGPU_CU_MASK sets (%gpu-env). A GPU left without a pair of units
is a software error at the spawn, or, on a processor with work group
processors, which enables units in pairs, the offload plugin's error when it
starts.
RUN: %gpu-env LIBOMPTARGET_AMDGPU_CU_MASK=4-7 %t2 gpu | FileCheck %S/process-spawn-at.m --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
RUN: not %gpu-env LIBOMPTARGET_AMDGPU_CU_MASK=0 %t2 gpu 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NOPAIR
NOPAIR: {{Software Error: process_spawn_at.spawn_summer_at: GPU 0 has no pair of compute units for processes, units 2N and 2N\+1|Mercury runtime: could not list liboffload's devices: .* enables compute units in pairs}}
